":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105835?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mduvall","html_url":"https://github.com/mduvall","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mduvall/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mduvall/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mduvall/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mduvall/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mduvall/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mduvall/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mduvall/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mduvall/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mduvall/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2013-12-02T04:35:12Z","updated_at":"2013-12-02T04:35:12Z","body":"Was working on converting to `SwitchCase` here, however getting the comments for a case will return the comments of the previous `case` as the leading comments. Maybe I'm missing something, but it seems ambiguous which nodes the comments will attach themselves to.\n\nExample:\n\n``` javascript\nswitch(foo) {\n  case \"bar\":\n    /* falls through */\n  case \"baz\":\n    qux();\n}\n```\n\nThe `SwitchCase` for `baz` will have comments that look like:\n\n``` javascript\n  { leading:\n   [ { type: 'Block',\n       value: ' falls through ',\n       range: [Object],\n       loc: [Object],\n       extendedRange: [Object] } ],\n  trailing: [] }\n```\n\nFor now I'll do a PR using the `SwitchStatement`, let me know if something seems weird here I can fix though - feels funky to be traversing over the cases.\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eslint/eslint/issues/comments/29594101/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"ev